{"containerCssClass":"mb-0 remove-parent-margin portfolio-metrics","markup":"        <section class=\"content-area-right-bottom-part mb-0 remove-parent-margin portfolio-metrics\" id=\"\" data-originalid=\"\">\r\n            <div class=\"row\">\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"col-lg-6\">\r\n            <h3 class=\"h2\">Fundamentals            <span class=\"d-block pt-2\">as of 11/02/2026</span>\r\n</h3>\r\n    <ul class=\"details\">\r\n            <li class=\"grey\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nYield to Worst        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Yield to Worst measures the lowest of either yield-to-maturity or yield-to-call date on every possible call date.\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n6.86                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li class=\"\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nYears to Maturity        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Years to Maturity is the period of time for which a financial instrument remains outstanding. Maturity refers to a finite time period at the end of which the financial instrument will cease to exist and the principal is repaid.\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n7.50                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li class=\"grey\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nEffective Duration (yrs)        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Effective Duration measures a bond's sensitivity to interest rate changes that reflects the change in a bond's price given a change in yield. This duration measure is appropriate for bonds with embedded options.\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n5.12                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li class=\"\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nCoupon        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Coupon is measured by weighting the coupon of each bond by its relative size in the portfolio. Coupons are fixed percentages paid on a fixed-income security on an annual basis.\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n6.29                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n\r\n    </ul>\r\n        <div class=\"description chart-disclaimer\">\r\n            Averages are market weighted. The yields presented do not represent the performance of the Fund. These statistics do not take into account fees and expenses associated with investments of the Fund.\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"col-lg-6\">\r\n            <h3 class=\"h2\">3-YR Risk Measures            <span class=\"d-block pt-2\">as of 09/30/2026</span>\r\n</h3>\r\n    <ul class=\"details\">\r\n            <li class=\"grey\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nBeta vs. S&P 500 Index        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Beta is a measure of sensitivity to market movements. \r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n0.31                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li class=\"\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nCorrelation vs. S&P 500 Index        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Correlation measures the extent of linear association between the ETF performance and the index performance. \r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n0.51                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li class=\"grey\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nVolatility (Standard Deviation)        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Volatility is the annualized standard deviation of monthly returns.\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n7.64                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li class=\"\">\r\n                        <div>\r\nSharpe Ratio        <span class=\"more-info-icon-svg-fund-pages\">\r\n                <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\">\r\n                    <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"10\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#6B696B\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"5\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                    <rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"2\" height=\"6\" fill=\"white\"/>\r\n                </svg>\r\n        </span>\r\n            <div class=\"subscription-tooltip-content\" style=\"display:none;\">\r\n                <div class=\"fund-explorer-block w-100\">\r\n                    Sharpe ratio measures risk-adjusted return, and represents the return less the risk free rate divided by the standard deviation. \r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n                        </div>\r\n                        <div>\r\n0.39                        </div>\r\n            </li>\r\n\r\n    </ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n            </div>\r\n        </section>\r\n","blockId":230678}